Correction to the commit message (2026-10-28): NULL also remains in
compiled code where it is passed as a variadic argument, e.g. the
terminating NULL of concat(..., NULL).  clang-tidy's
modernize-use-nullptr deliberately leaves those alone because no pointer
conversion takes place there.  After these commits, clang-tidy reports 0
remaining modernize-use-nullptr warnings across all 105 .cc files.
